# transport hard cap. Single diagnosed fix committed before the one-shot read re-execution;
# the flown run directory was not touched.
#
# CORRECTION (2026-08-19, before the read): the crashing meeting is TS3004d, not TS3004b --
# the slice bounds 2035.2585/2160.5665 match TS3004d's oracle turn-group geometry exactly
# (group [2035.272, 2136.408] + half of a 48.317 s silence gap), and TS3004b's oracle plan
# builds cleanly at HEAD. Attempt 2 (with audio-derived inputs wired, commit ec829d4) hit the
# identical violation because TS3004d has ZERO detected energy-pause transitions, exposing the
# real root cause: the slicer's INTERIOR gap-midpoint tiling was not room-capped (the e627f8e
# edge fix covered only the first/last slice). See attempt-2-transportbound-crash.log and the
# slicer fix commit that follows ec829d4.

